  "answer": "Fixed. Here's what was wrong:\n\n**Root cause:** The backend delete endpoint is `DELETE /api/v1/cart/{code}/product/{sku}` \u2014 it expects the product **SKU** as the path variable. But `deleteFromCart` built the URL with `item.id` (the numeric product DB id). The backend facade matches line items with `product.getSku().equals(sku)`, so the numeric id never matched any line, no item was removed, and the endpoint still returned success \u2014 which is exactly the \"nothing happens\" symptom (the local Redux update even makes it look like it worked until a refresh brings it back).\n\n**Fix (one line in `src/redux/actions/cartActions.js`):** changed `item.id` \u2192 `item.sku`, the same field `addToCart` already uses for the identical `product` parameter.\n\nVerified the URL now resolves to `cart/{cartId}/product/{sku}?store=\u2026`, matching `BasketEndpoint.removeLine`. CRLF line endings were preserved; `git diff` shows only that single line changed.\n\n**Files used:**\n- `src/redux/actions/cartActions.js` (the edit)\n- `src/util/webService.js` and `src/util/constant.js` (URL/HTTP layer)\n- Backend at `~/code/benchmark/okf-local/pr2`: `BasketEndpoint.java` (DELETE mapping), `ShoppingCartFacadeImpl.java` (SKU-based matching), and the cart mappers (`ReadableShoppingCartMapper.java`, `ReadableMinimalProductMapper.java`) to confirm cart items expose both `id` and `sku`.",
